  "text": "To find the point \\( E \\) such that the four small triangles \\( AEB \\), \\( AEC \\), \\( BED \\), and \\( CED \\) all have equal perimeters, we need to identify the midpoint of the diagonals of the parallelogram \\( ABCD \\). This point will be equidistant from all the sides of the parallelogram and will have the property that the perimeters of the triangles formed will be equal. The midpoint of the diagonals of a parallelogram is the intersection point of the diagonals.\n\nFirst, we calculate the coordinates of the midpoint \\( E \\) of the diagonals \\( AC \\) and \\( BD \\).\n\n1. Calculate the midpoint of \\( AC \\):\nThe coordinates of \\( A \\) are \\( (2, 3) \\) and \\( C \\) are \\( (8, 9) \\).\n\n\\[\nE = \\left( \\frac{2+8}{2}, \\frac{3+9}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{10}{2}, \\frac{12}{2} \\right) = (5, 6)\n\\]\n\nSo, the coordinates of point \\( E \\) are \\( (5, 6) \\).\n\n2. Verify the result by checking the distances from \\( E \\) to the vertices \\( A, B, C, \\) and \\( D \\) and ensuring the perimeters of the triangles are equal.\n\nHowever, we need to check the distances and perimeters:\n\\[\n(x - 2)^2 + (y - 3)^2 = (5 - 2)^2 + (6 - 3)^2\n\\]\n\\[\n(x - 6)^2 + (y - 5)^2 = (5 - 6)^2 + (6 - 5)^2\n\\]\n\\[\n(x - 8)^2 + (y - 9)^2 = (5 - 8)^2 + (6 - 9)^2\n\\]\n\\[\n(x - 4)^2 + (y - 7)^2 = (5 - 4)^2 + (6 - 7)^2\n\\]\n\nThe coordinates of the midpoint ensure the equal perimeter condition. So, we can directly calculate \\( 5x + 2y \\):\n\nIf \\( (x,y) = (5,6) \\):\n\\[\n5x + 2y = 5(5) + 2(6) = 25 + 12 = 37\n\\]\n\nSo, the value of \\( 5x + 2y \\) is \\(\\boxed{37}\\).",
